    <!--
        SK DPH tax-report tags (18.0 backport of Odoo 19.0 core l10n_sk)
        ================================================================
        Odoo 19.0 CE ``l10n_sk`` ships ``data/tax_report.xml`` (an
        ``account.report`` whose ``tax_tags`` expressions auto-create the DPH
        report tags 01..29 + lettered sub-codes) plus a
        ``repartition_line_ids/tag_ids`` column on ``account.tax-sk.csv`` that
        binds those tags to the SK taxes. Odoo 18.0 CE ``l10n_sk`` ships
        NEITHER — the tags do not exist and the SK taxes carry no tax tags, so
        every ``kind='tags'`` VAT/KV/EC return line evaluates to 0.

        We are CE-clean: our statutory filing (l10n_sk_vat_return / _kv_dph /
        _ec_sales) reads ``account.account.tag._get_tax_tags(code, SK)``, NOT
        the EE report engine, so we only need the *tags* to exist — not the
        ``account.report`` UI. We therefore create every DPH tag here with a
        stable XML-ID (``tag_sk_<code>``) and reference those XML-IDs from the
        ``@template('sk','account.tax')`` data (see models/ and
        data/template/account.tax-sk.csv). 18.0's ``_deref_account_tags`` runs
        only on the CSV parsed by core's None-code loader, NOT on our template
        data, so bare tag names would crash in ``deref_values`` — hence XML-IDs.

        Only the "+" (tax_negate=False) tag of each code is created: our
        evaluator resolves a code via ``=like '_<code>'`` (matches either sign)
        and encodes the display sign in the version-data formula, so a single
        positive tag per code is sufficient and unambiguous.
    -->
    <record id="tag_sk_01" model="account.account.tag">
        <field name="name">+01</field>
        <field name="applicability">taxes</field>
        <field name="country_id" ref="base.sk"/>
    </record>
    <record id="tag_sk_02" model="account.account.tag">
